Track 1: Did You Salt the Broth Before Sunrise?
- Story & Context: It began during an unseasonably damp October dawn at Ssanggye Hermitage, when sound engineer Min-jae spilled boiling anchovy broth directly across an open patchbay while Brother Jin-woo was charting his sleep-visions into modular oscillation waveforms. The sudden short-circuit spat out an erratic, warm sub-harmonic hum that vibrated through the floorboards, prompting percussionist Batu to seize her goat-hide djembe and instinctively counter the low rumble with polyrhythmic open slaps. Lim entered the steam-filled kitchen clutching a tin mug, coughing into the microphone before improvising the now-legendary opening falsetto hook, "Leave the flame on simmer till the cedar wood bends." The tape kept rolling through the scorched smell of kelp and melting solder, cementing the first true sonic blueprint of the Silt-Velour sound.
