Track 2: Garlic Cloves Bruise the Output
- Story & Context: Recorded in the cluttered pantry of an old Mapo-gu rowhouse, this confession tracks Eun-ji Lim's exhausted ritual of peeling mountain garlic while obsessing over an unanswered transatlantic telephone call. Between the rhythmic thud of her chef's knife against wet hinoki wood, she dialed in a heavily fluttered 1974 tape delay, matching her breathy microtonal vocal run to the lingering decay of Brother Jin-woo's transcribed nightmare-frequency tape loops. Batu locked into a muted djembe heel-tip rhythm using her bare hands, deliberately bruising her knuckles against the raw hide when the take crossed into its seventh unedited minute. Over the stinging fragrance of crushed alliums and overheating vacuum tubes, Lim finally delivers her breaking-point vocal run, singing "You swallowed my winter but left the bowl bone-dry."
